{%- comment -%}
  price-badge — the shared price/discount badge component. Signature is
  frozen:

    {%- render 'price-badge', price: <cents>, compare: <cents>, layout: 'card' | 'pdp' -%}

  Badge only when compare > price. Percentage = (compare − price) × 100 /
  compare, integer-rounded — computed from THIS product's own compareAtPrice,
  never a storewide constant, so the number is always real and therefore
  looks credible (an odd "−36%" rather than a round marketing number). No
  anchor → plain price, no strikethrough, no badge — nothing invented.

  Money formatting is NOT decided here. All three prices go through
  `render 'price'`, which is the one place settings.price_show_cents is read —
  this snippet used to hardcode money_without_trailing_zeros, which made it the
  one surface that could not follow the setting. The frozen signature is the
  three parameters above; the money filter was never part of it.

  Card styles `.pb--card`, PDP styles `.pb--pdp`, both now in theme.css (the
  *-extras.css files are folded into it). Never add rules for the other
  layout's class from here.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign has_discount = false
  if compare and compare > price
    assign has_discount = true
    assign pct = compare | minus: price | times: 100.0 | divided_by: compare | round
  endif
-%}
<span class="pb pb--{{ layout }}">
  {%- if has_discount -%}
    <s>{% render 'price', amount: compare %}</s>
    <span class="price--sale">{% render 'price', amount: price %}</span>
    <span class="pb__badge">&minus;{{ pct }}%</span>
  {%- else -%}
    {% render 'price', amount: price %}
  {%- endif -%}
</span>
